{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — one accordion row inside the product panel.

  Aloha, 3 September 2026: "Longer information organised through restrained
  accordion rows […] Less copy visible within the first screen."

  Luxe's native `collapsible_tab` block already gives an accordion row, but it
  can only hold richtext or a page — it cannot hold a metafield-driven component
  such as the Material Record. This snippet closes that gap WITHOUT introducing a
  second accordion style beside Luxe's, which is precisely the visual busyness
  Aloha is asking us to remove.

  It emits Luxe's own accordion markup, exactly:

      <div class="accordion"><button class="accordion-title">…</button>
                             <div class="accordion-panel">…</div></div>

  assets/global.js binds every `.accordion-title` on the page at DOMContentLoaded
  and animates `heading.nextElementSibling`, so a row built here behaves like a
  native one — same open/close, same height animation, same ARIA — with no
  JavaScript of our own and no fork of the section.

  `content` is already-rendered HTML, so capture it at the call site:

    {%- capture record -%}{%- render 'ha-material-record', product: product, full: true,
         hide_eyebrow: true, hide_title: true, hide_intro: true -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- render 'ha-panel-row', id: 'record', title: 'Material Record', content: record -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign row_id = id | default: 'row'
  assign panel_id = 'ha-panel-' | append: row_id
  assign button_id = panel_id | append: '-button'
  assign is_open = false
  if open
    assign is_open = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if content != blank -%}
  <div class="accordion ha-panel-row">
    <button
      class="accordion-title{% if is_open %} active{% endif %}"
      type="button"
      aria-expanded="{{ is_open }}"
      aria-controls="{{ panel_id }}"
      id="{{ button_id }}"
    >
      <span>{{ title }}</span>
      <div class="accordion-icons-wrapper">
        <div class="accordion-icon-open">{% if settings.accordion_icon == 'plus' %}{% render 'icon-plus' %}{% else %}{% render 'icon-caret' %}{% endif %}</div>
        <div class="accordion-icon-close">{% if settings.accordion_icon == 'plus' %}{% render 'icon-minus' %}{% else %}{% render 'icon-caret' %}{% endif %}</div>
      </div>
    </button>
    <div
      class="accordion-panel{% if is_open %} panel-open{% endif %}"
      id="{{ panel_id }}"
      aria-hidden="{% if is_open %}false{% else %}true{% endif %}"
      aria-labelledby="{{ button_id }}"
    >
      {{ content }}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
